Subject: win32u/user32: hide the menu bar's alt-key mnemonic
 underlines

Real Windows only shows these once Alt is pressed (the
WM_UPDATEUISTATE/UISF_HIDEACCEL keyboard-cues system); this Wine tree
never implements that message handling at all (confirmed: no
WM_UPDATEUISTATE/WM_QUERYUISTATE/WM_CHANGEUISTATE handling outside
tests), so the top-level menu bar always draws them, unlike real
Windows or macOS - reported as issue 35 point 6 ("is it possible to
remove the underlines from the Wine menu bar").

Implementing the full Alt-to-reveal toggle is a much larger feature
(global UI-state tracking, Alt key press/release wiring, propagation
through every window). DT_HIDEPREFIX on the menu bar's DrawTextW call
gets the actual visual result asked for - permanently hidden, & still
handled as an escape rather than drawn literally - without any of
that. Scoped to the menu bar only; popup/dropdown items keep their
mnemonics, where Alt-key in-menu navigation is still commonly used.

DT_HIDEPREFIX turned out to be a dead flag in this tree: defined in
winuser.h and mentioned in a text.c comment, but dlls/user32/text.c's
actual underline-drawing site (TEXT_DrawUnderscore's call, gated on
prefix_offset) only ever checked DT_NOPREFIX, never DT_HIDEPREFIX -
so setting it alone had no visible effect, confirmed by testing.
DT_NOPREFIX isn't the right substitute either: it stops '&' from
being treated as an escape at all, which would show a literal '&' in
the text instead of just hiding the underline. Fixed by gating the
underscore draw itself on DT_HIDEPREFIX too, leaving '&'-stripping
and prefix-offset tracking (unaffected by this flag pre-existing)
exactly as before.
---
 dlls/user32/text.c |  2 +-
 dlls/win32u/menu.c | 10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/user32/text.c b/dlls/user32/text.c
index 114d069..56d07de 100644
--- a/dlls/user32/text.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/text.c
@@ -1018,7 +1018,7 @@ INT WINAPI DrawTextExW( HDC hdc, LPWSTR str, INT i_count,
                                  ((flags & DT_RTLREADING) ? ETO_RTLREADING : 0),
                                  rect, str, len_seg, NULL ))
                     goto done;
-                if (prefix_offset != -1 && prefix_offset < len_seg)
+                if (prefix_offset != -1 && prefix_offset < len_seg && !(flags & DT_HIDEPREFIX))
                 {
                     TEXT_DrawUnderscore (hdc, xseg, y + tm.tmAscent + 1, str, prefix_offset, (flags & DT_NOCLIP) ? NULL : rect);
                 }
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/menu.c b/dlls/win32u/menu.c
index 08b1665..1ff3403 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/menu.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/menu.c
@@ -2677,8 +2677,16 @@ static void draw_menu_item( HWND hwnd, struct menu *menu, HWND owner, HDC hdc,
     {
         int i;
         HFONT prev_font = 0;
+        /* Real Windows hides these mnemonic underlines until Alt is pressed
+         * (the WM_UPDATEUISTATE/UISF_HIDEACCEL "keyboard cues" system) - not
+         * implemented anywhere in this Wine tree (confirmed: no handling of
+         * WM_UPDATEUISTATE/WM_QUERYUISTATE/WM_CHANGEUISTATE outside tests),
+         * so without DT_HIDEPREFIX the top-level bar always shows them,
+         * unlike either real Windows' default or macOS. Scoped to the menu
+         * bar itself (issue 35 point 6); popup/dropdown items keep theirs,
+         * where Alt-key navigation within an open menu is still used. */
         UINT format = menu_bar ?
-            DT_CENTER | DT_VCENTER | DT_SINGLELINE :
+            DT_CENTER | DT_VCENTER | DT_SINGLELINE | DT_HIDEPREFIX :
             DT_LEFT | DT_VCENTER | DT_SINGLELINE;
 
         if (!(menu->dwStyle & MNS_CHECKORBMP))
